---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Earnometry — Make sense of the numbers." description="Free calculators and practical guides for YouTube creators. Understand earnings, RPM, view targets and sponsorship pricing with clear assumptions.">
  <section class="home-hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">A little clarity goes a long way</p>
    <h1 id="home-title">Make sense of<br />the <span>numbers.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Free calculators and practical guides for YouTube creators. Understand your earnings, RPM, view targets and sponsorship pricing.</p>
    <a class="button" href="/tools/youtube-money-calculator" data-analytics-cta="home_youtube_hero">Estimate your YouTube earnings <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    <p class="quiet-note">Free to use. No signup needed.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="featured" aria-labelledby="featured-title">
    <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Start with a useful number</p><h2 id="featured-title">Your creator income,<br />with clearer assumptions.</h2></div>
    <div class="tool-list">
    <article class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-card-top"><span class="pill">For creators</span><span class="tool-symbol" aria-hidden="true">÷</span></div>
      <h3><a href="/tools/youtube-money-calculator" data-analytics-cta="home_youtube_title">YouTube Money Calculator</a></h3>
      <p>Estimate revenue from your long-form and Shorts views using your own RPM assumptions. Explore a planning range and views needed for your income target.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/tools/youtube-money-calculator" data-analytics-cta="home_youtube_card">Estimate YouTube revenue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-card-top"><span class="pill">For creators</span><span class="tool-symbol" aria-hidden="true">÷</span></div>
      <h3><a href="/tools/sponsorship-rate-calculator" data-analytics-cta="home_sponsorship_title">Creator Sponsorship<br class="desktop-break" /> Rate Calculator</a></h3>
      <p>Turn your average views and deal details into an estimate you can understand. Adjust your assumptions and see exactly how the numbers add up.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/tools/sponsorship-rate-calculator" data-analytics-cta="home_sponsorship_card">Open the calculator <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-card-top"><span class="pill">Guide</span><span class="tool-symbol" aria-hidden="true">?</span></div>
      <h3><a href="/guides/how-many-youtube-views-to-make-1000" data-analytics-cta="home_guide_title">How Many YouTube Views Do You Need to Make $1,000?</a></h3>
      <p>Work backward from a $1,000 revenue goal. See the formula, compare hypothetical RPMs, and calculate the view count for your own channel.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/guides/how-many-youtube-views-to-make-1000" data-analytics-cta="home_guide_card">Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-home" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Practical by design</p><h2 id="about-title">Useful tools.<br />Clear assumptions.</h2></div>
    <div class="about-copy"><p>Earnometry helps YouTube creators work through the numbers behind their channels. Start with a calculator, understand the method, and use the result to inform your next decision.</p><p class="muted">Explore YouTube revenue, view targets and sponsorship pricing with your own assumptions.</p></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
